 "notes": "All four kinds kept. Jukebox: Rock-Ola Harley-Davidson models became versions of the Rock-Ola archetype; Filben Maestro kept in m. Compact hi-fi: added Denon D-M41 (maker page); Beocenter as archetype. Karaoke trimmed from 7 Singing Machine models to 5 (dropped Singcast One and Ultimate WiFi Karaoke Party as near-duplicates). Left out, not attested on a fetched page: Grundig and Blaupunkt radiograms (museum record timed out), Beosystem, AMI jukeboxes (only named), Yamaha MusicCast and Marantz M-CR612 systems. SK 4 is listed under Braun radio-phonographs; the fetched Core77 page treats it mainly as a record player."
